content.text:
Oops, my newString accidentally removed the ret-label/ret-coords/ret-status? No — those are defined in the base section at lines 555-561, still present. My replacement only affected the media block. Good.

Wait, I need to verify the base reticle styles remain intact. Yes, they were before line 700.

Now fix mobile logo and menu-inner. At max-width 620 currently:
```
.logo { font-size: 19vw; }
.menu-inner { padding: 0 22px; }
```
But `.menu-inner` width remains min(680px,88vw) from 1100 block = 346px; adding padding 22px each side makes content 302px, but box-sizing border-box so content 302. The logo overflow beyond. Set:
```
.menu-inner { padding: 0 20px; width: 100%; }
.logo { font-size: clamp(40px, 13.2vw, 72px); letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
```
At 393: 13.2vw = 51.9px. Width ~9*0.66*51.9 = 308px. Content width 353. Fits. At 360: 47.5px -> 282px, content 320. Fits.

Also on very small heights, menu content may overflow. We could add `overflow-y: auto` on .screen, but body fixed. The menu-inner at 659 height fits. In landscape mobile (852x393), the menu vertical content won't fit at all. Need to handle landscape mobile too! The menu is tall (~540px) but landscape height 393. It will be clipped. Need responsive for short viewports. Perhaps use `@media (max-height: 560px)` to scale down menu: reduce logo, brief margins, hide brief? Let's design:

For landscape phone (height ~393):
- menu-inner should compact: logo ~48px, brief hidden or smaller, controls hidden on coarse anyway, settings compact, footer hidden.
- Deploy button smaller.
- Menu should fit: eyebrow 10 + logo 40 + sub 12 + brief maybe 2 lines 40 + button 60 + settings 50 = ~250. Fits.

Add:
```
@media (max-height: 560px) {
  .menu-inner { width: min(620px, 80vw); }
  .logo { font-size: clamp(34px, 7.2vw, 60px); }
  .brief { display:none; }
  .logo-sub { margin-top: 6px; }
  .controls-grid { display:none; }
  .settings-row { margin-top: 14px; padding-top: 10px; }
  .menu-foot { display:none; }
  .btn-primary { min-width: 230px; padding: 12px 24px 10px; }
  .btn-label { font-size: 16px; }
}
```
Also menu-reticle hidden at max-width 900 — landscape width 852 -> hidden. Fine.

For the pause/gameover panels at short height, they may overflow. Add `max-height: 92vh; overflow-y: auto;` to .panel. That's safe.

Also mobile touch UI bottom: check later.

Let me apply.

