content.text:
The mobile capture (390x844 portrait, desktop pointer) is a mess: HUD overlaps at bottom because the touch HUD overrides only apply under pointer coarse, and this capture is desktop pointer at portrait size. The banner "INCOMING WAVE 01" overlaps health/ammo because the viewport is narrow and the hud-bottom flex layout is not adjusted for non-touch portrait. Also the deploy started and the game is running in portrait without rotate hint (since pointer fine). On an actual phone, pointer coarse triggers rotate hint. But the official capture uses a desktop context at 390x844, so it exposes this. We should make the layout work even at narrow widths with pointer fine. Since `@media (max-width: 820px)` already exists but the banner overlaps because of the wave-center and bottom blocks. Let's fix the narrow non-touch layout.

At 390 width, `.hud-bottom` is flex with health-block width 46vw (from max-width 620) = 179, weapon-block min-width 120, gap 30, left/right 18 => total 179+120+30+36=365 fits barely. But the wave banner is absolutely positioned within wave-center (flex:1) which has almost no width, so it's centered at bottom and overlaps both. In the capture, banner is huge (34px) and centered at y~800, over health/ammo. On mobile touch, banner would also overlap? In mobile-play2, the wave banner wasn't visible (had faded), but "NEXT WAVE IN 7" at bottom center was okay. The banner could overlap health/ammo in touch layout too because hud-bottom is still the same and health/ammo moved up, so banner at bottom center is clear! Because health/ammo moved up. But for non-touch narrow, health/ammo are at bottom, causing overlap with banner.

Also on portrait, the HUD top is fine: wave center, stats right (mission hidden), but ammo at bottom-right and health bottom-left. The banner overlaps.

We need a proper narrow-screen layout. Option: for max-width 620 (or 820), move the wave banner up above the bottom HUD, e.g. `#wave-banner { bottom: 70px; }` or place it centered at 40% of screen. Since banner is transient, put it at `bottom: 110px` on narrow screens. Also `#wave-timer` could move up. And health/ammo at bottom remain. Let's add to max-width 620:

```
#wave-banner { bottom: 96px; }
#banner-title { font-size: 34px; }
#wave-timer { position: absolute; bottom: 86px; }
```

But #wave-timer is a child of .wave-center (flex:1), not absolutely positioned; it sits in flow. The .wave-center is centered horizontally at bottom of hud-bottom; with no width, it may overflow. `#wave-timer` could be `position: fixed; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); bottom: calc(92px + safe-b)`. The banner is absolute bottom 0 of wave-center; set bottom 80px.

However, in touch layout, health/ammo moved up to 172/66, so bottom center is clear. Setting banner bottom 96 would put it in the middle, maybe over the gun viewmodel, but fine. Actually on touch landscape, the banner currently appears at bottom center (above bottom edge) and may overlap the touch buttons? The banner is centered and buttons at right/left, so clear. We don't want to move it up unnecessarily for touch landscape. Apply only to `@media (max-width: 620px)` (portrait phones) or `@media (max-width: 820px) and (orientation: portrait)`. Since touch landscape is 844 wide, max-width 620 won't apply. Good.

Also the mobile capture at 390x844 non-touch shows "VITALS 150" overlapping "WAVE 01" etc. Moving banner up fixes.

Additionally, on narrow non-touch, the touch UI isn't shown, but there are no controls; that's fine for capture.

Also, the mobile capture's health/ammo at bottom: health block at left 18 bottom 16, ammo at right 18 bottom 16. The banner center overlaps. Moving banner to bottom 96 clears.

Also note the ammo block's "MK-7 VANGUARD" hidden at max-width 620, good. The ammo "30 / 210" is at bottom right, with pips. Fine.

Let's add:
```
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  #wave-banner { bottom: 86px; }
  #banner-title { font-size: 32px; }
  #banner-sub { font-size: 8px; }
  #wave-timer { position: fixed; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); bottom: calc(82px + var(--safe-b)); }
}
```
Wait #wave-timer is shown during intermission and sits at bottom center; if we make it fixed bottom 82, it will be above health/ammo? Health/ammo bottom 16, height ~50 => top ~778 at 844. Bottom 82 => timer at y ~740, above. Good.

But for touch portrait, rotate hint covers; irrelevant. For touch landscape (844 width), max-width 620 doesn't apply; timer at bottom center and health/ammo are up, so fine.

Also, the mobile capture shows the "INCOMING WAVE 01" banner with kicker "INCOMING" overlapping the health/ammo. Moving up 86px should clear (banner height ~70, bottom 86 => top 688, health top ~778). Good.

Let's implement.

