There's a bug: the pause screen says "PRESS ESC TO RESUME" but Escape doesn't resume. Also P pauses but P doesn't resume (only if playing). We should implement Escape/P to resume when paused. But careful: when pointer lock is active, pressing Escape triggers browser pointerlock exit, and our keydown may or may not fire. On pause, pointer lock already exited. So pressing Escape while paused should resume. Add:

```
window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (e.code === 'KeyP' || e.code === 'Escape') {
    if (this.state === 'playing') this.pause()
    else if (this.state === 'paused') this.resume()
  }
})
```
But pressing Escape while playing normally exits pointer lock and triggers pause via lock change; also keydown might fire and pause directly (same result). Fine. However, when game over, Escape shouldn't do anything. Fine.

Also, clicking Resume calls requestLock; pointer lock requires a user gesture, and click provides it. Good. Pressing Escape to resume calls requestLock from keydown (user gesture), allowed.

Let's implement. Also update the pause hint to "PRESS ESC OR P TO RESUME". Check index.html for pause hint text.

